{"answers":[],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-9","impact":1,"impactReason":"This is a scope and run-planning decision, not a change to product data or permissions.","options":["Approve all 22 requirements as one run.","Reject this run and identify which requirements to cut."],"reason":"The request describes the full feedlot solution, so approving it preserves the requested scope.","recommended":"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.","score":3,"spans":[],"text":"Should all 22 requirements be approved as one run, or should some requirements be cut?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-10","impact":3,"impactReason":"Feeding saves write activity records and affect inventory consumption and costs.","options":["Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.","Add a stable save idempotency key and authoritative status lookup; retry only after the service confirms no event was saved.","Keep using matching event fields in a refreshed activity list to infer whether the save succeeded."],"reason":"The request asks for feeding activity logging and reliable inventory handling, but does not ask for new idempotency or status-lookup machinery.","recommended":"Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"How should the app handle a feeding save that times out when it cannot reliably tell whether the event was saved?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-11","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines which records contribute to operational totals and what users see in dashboards and summaries.","options":["Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.","Require the service to return dashboard and yard-summary aggregates that exclude sample records.","Calculate these aggregates client-side from returned records, excluding sample records."],"reason":"The request asks for sample data and aggregate views, but does not require sample records to be excluded from those views.","recommended":"Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should dashboard and yard-summary aggregates be guaranteed to exclude sample records, even when the service returns aggregates mixed with operational data?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"AC-11.8–11.9 treats matching event fields in a refreshed activity list as proof of whether a timed-out save succeeded, so an older identical event can be mistaken for the new save and a delayed or omitted event can lead to a duplicate feeding and inventory decrement.","reqId":"REQ-11","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-20.7 requires sample-free dashboard and yard-summary totals even when the response mixes sample and operational records, while REQ-15 and REQ-21 require displaying returned summary and aggregate values, leaving no consistent client behavior if those returned aggregates include sample data.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-13.2 defines an unavailable state only for the projected ship date, leaving FCR and cost of gain without a display state when a lot has no usable weight gain or feeding history and their denominators are zero or missing.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-19.1 requires only whatever profitability values happen to be returned, without naming any required profit, revenue, or margin value, so a list with no profitability analysis can satisfy the criterion.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-15.2 checks that the selected ranking measure is shown but not that lots are ordered by it, so an unchanged or incorrectly ordered best-and-worst list can pass when FCR, ADG, and cost-of-gain rankings differ.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-20.8 adds exports of operational inventory and yard-summary views even though REQ-6 and REQ-21 only request viewing those screens and the requested exports concern reports, expanding the export surface without supporting intent.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":4,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-6.2 covers only successful inventory edits, receipts, adjustments, and wastage-setting changes, with no screen behavior for a refused or failed submission despite those actions changing stock and future feeding availability.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"}],"lint":[{"blocking":true,"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","fails":["This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."],"passed":false},{"blocking":true,"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","fails":[],"hint":"Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes.","passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":["Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal overflow or page scrolling, and provide touch controls of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels on narrow screens."]}},"problemOf":{"Q-10":[2],"Q-11":[3],"Q-9":[1]},"problems":[{"kind":"lint","text":"L9 size: This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-11","text":"AC-11.8–11.9 treats matching event fields in a refreshed activity list as proof of whether a timed-out save succeeded, so an older identical event can be mistaken for the new save and a delayed or omitted event can lead to a duplicate feeding and inventory decrement."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-20","text":"AC-20.7 requires sample-free dashboard and yard-summary totals even when the response mixes sample and operational records, while REQ-15 and REQ-21 require displaying returned summary and aggregate values, leaving no consistent client behavior if those returned aggregates include sample data."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal overflow or page scrolling, and provide touch controls of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels on narrow screens."}],"round":1,"settled":[],"spec":{"assumptions":["Procurement and receiving demo data is imported through a documented mock adapter; a live connector awaits identification of the source system and interface.","Repeated source imports are matched by source identifiers; PO lines and lots can split across lots and pens while retaining allocated animal quantities.","Forecasts use configurable yard target-weight and expected-gain defaults with optional lot-specific overrides.","Configured wastage applies to estimates and projections; actual known wastage is a separate movement, while actual stock consumption is based on delivered quantity.","Ration optimization compares candidate mixes with user-selected nutritional requirements, displays the lowest-cost qualifying mix, and saves only when the user chooses.","A saved plan remains unchanged and is flagged for review after relevant inputs change; an authorized planner confirms or regenerates it.","When stock is insufficient, the feeding save is refused and the web app presents the returned error.","Feed calculations use as-fed quantities; feed totals are converted to pounds for feed-to-gain metrics and dry matter is used for nutrition calculations.","A projected ship date uses the current date plus remaining target weight divided by positive ADG and is unavailable without positive ADG.","Date-range report metrics use feeding and weight records in the selected range; sex is retained when supplied and its filter is unavailable for records without sex data.","Dashboard lot rankings use a user-selected measure; dashboards remain summary-only and lot/report screens provide detail.","Predictive suggestions are explainable rule-based recommendations and do not change saved plans unless a user chooses an action.","Sample records remain distinguishable from operational records, duplicate loading is prevented or surfaced through the returned result, and reset or replacement requires confirmation.","Yard summary ADG and cost of gain use aggregate values across included active lots.","Screen actions and displayed values follow permissions returned for the signed-in user; role descriptions do not establish additional role names or permissions.","Lot profitability is presented as an on-screen filtered list with CSV export rather than a custom report builder.","The API is authoritative for server-side calculations and permissions; the web app displays returned values and refusal messages."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 360 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, 100% of pages render without horizontal overflow; interactive controls at 360 px width have a minimum 44-by-44 CSS-pixel target.","text":"Every page shall render responsively at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"At viewport widths 320 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, horizontal page overflow is 0 px; at 320 px width, each touch control is at least 44 × 44 CSS px.","text":"Every web page shall remain usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling, and touch controls at the narrow viewport shall have a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 horizontal overflow at viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1440 CSS px; primary touch controls are at least 44 × 44 CSS px at 320 CSS px.","text":"Every web-app page shall render without horizontal page overflow at phone, tablet, and desktop reference widths."}],"outOfScope":["A live procurement-system connector is deferred; the demo uses a documented mock-data import adapter.","Durable persistence and database migration behavior for imported records, mappings, inventory, rations, plans, feeding events, and weight measurements are API-side and not specified by these web requirements.","Authoritative server-side calculation and update rules for inventory movements, ration nutrition and cost, feed-plan quantities, lot rollups, forecast values, and feed-to-gain metrics are not specified by these web requirements.","Authorization enforcement, import identifier matching and deduplication, stock sufficiency decisions, and authoritative yard/profitability data filtering are API-side; these web requirements cover controls, displayed responses, and export contents."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service accepts the submitted credentials and returns the user and permissions","id":"AC-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned operational landing page and navigation actions allowed by the returned permissions","when":"The user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service refuses the submitted credentials","id":"AC-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error message and remains on the sign-in page","when":"The user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"An authenticated screen displays protected data and the session expires or a protected request receives HTTP 401","id":"AC-1.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen returns to sign-in and no protected page data remains displayed","when":"The web app handles the expired session or 401 response"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in, send the submitted credentials to the sign-in service, display the resulting landing page or authentication error, render navigation and actions according to the signed-in user's returned permissions, and clear authenticated page data and return to sign-in when an authenticated session expires or a protected request returns HTTP 401.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-9","Q-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operationally authorized user opens the import screen and mock adapter records are available","id":"AC-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each available record's vendor, source identifier, cost, head count, animal weight, breed, age, source, purchase-order, and receiving fields","when":"The user previews the source records"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user has selected mock source records","id":"AC-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The import request contains the selected source records and the screen displays the response status, imported-record list, and returned created or updated counts when supplied","when":"The user submits the import"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens the import screen","id":"AC-2.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays imported records and does not show an enabled import action","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"Where mock procurement and receiving import is available, the feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users preview and submit selected records through the documented mock-data adapter and display the returned import result and source fields.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-23","ASM-24","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An imported PO line is allocated across multiple lots and a lot is allocated across multiple pens","id":"AC-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationship with its allocated animal quantity","when":"The mapping screen renders the returned mappings"},{"given":"A mapping response contains pen information","id":"AC-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each mapped pen's ID, capacity, current animal count, and mapped allocation quantity","when":"The mapping screen renders the response"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user changes mapping quantities, or a user without operational access opens the mapping screen","id":"AC-3.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved mapping values returned by the service, and for a user without operational access it displays existing mappings without mapping-change actions","when":"The authorized user saves mappings or the other user's screen renders using returned permissions"},{"given":"An edited allocation conflicts with a PO line's returned head count or a pen's returned capacity and the mapping service refuses the save","id":"AC-3.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned error and the last saved mapping values remain displayed","when":"The user submits the mapping changes"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to one or more pens, retain allocated animal quantities, and display the resulting traceability and pen information.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-25","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The import response identifies source records as matched to existing records","id":"AC-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the matched record list and response status without displaying those records as newly created duplicates","when":"The repeated import completes"},{"given":"A repeated-import response updates a PO line's head count below its existing mapped allocation quantities and returns an allocation conflict","id":"AC-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the matched record, returned head count, existing mapped quantities, and an allocation-conflict flag without presenting the record as a new duplicate","when":"The repeated import completes"}],"ears":"When an operational user repeats an import containing previously imported source-system identifiers, the feedlot web app shall display the import result for the matched records returned by the import service without presenting them as newly created duplicates, and flag returned allocation conflicts when an updated head count is below existing mapped quantities.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-24","Q-3"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and a lot-specific override","id":"AC-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned incoming data, target weight, expected gain rate, projected market date, and forecast basis using the lot-specific override","when":"A user opens the lot forecast"},{"given":"A lot forecast has no positive gain rate available","id":"AC-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The projected date field displays an unavailable value on the screen","when":"The user opens the forecast"},{"given":"An authorized manager changes a yard default or lot-specific override, or a user without manager authorization opens forecast settings","id":"AC-5.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned forecast values for saved changes, and does not show assumption-edit actions to a user without manager authorization","when":"The manager saves the assumption or the other user's screen renders"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display market-date and target-weight forecasts from incoming animal data and configured yard defaults, use lot-specific overrides when present, show a forecast as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and expose forecast-assumption editing only to authorized managers.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-3","ASM-33","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory response contains feed items and stock movements","id":"AC-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, wastage setting when returned, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"A user opens the inventory screen"},{"given":"An authorized inventory user records a receipt or adjustment, edits an item, or changes wastage settings","id":"AC-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved inventory record and stock-movement values returned by the service","when":"The user submits the change"},{"given":"A user has inventory viewing access but lacks inventory-edit access","id":"AC-6.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays inventory values and does not show enabled item, receipt, adjustment, or wastage-edit actions","when":"The user opens inventory"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display feed inventory items and stock movements and let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts or adjustments, and change wastage settings, while displaying inventory details to users with viewing access.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-28","ASM-34","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The projection response contains available stock, upcoming saved feed plans, and wastage-adjusted estimates","id":"AC-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned projected consumption and closing or remaining inventory for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons, along with the configured wastage ratio","when":"A user selects each supported projection horizon"},{"given":"The projection response has no saved upcoming feed plans for an item","id":"AC-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the response's empty-data state for that item's projected inventory","when":"A user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"The inventory service returns a known actual-wastage movement and delivered-feed consumption","id":"AC-7.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen lists actual wastage as a separate movement from delivered-feed consumption","when":"A user views the stock movement list"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons using saved upcoming feed plans and configured wastage, while presenting known actual wastage separately from delivered-feed consumption.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-27","ASM-28"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized ration manager creates or revises a ration","id":"AC-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays fields for ration name and type, ingredients, proportions, intended animal type or weight range, dry matter, energy, and cost per unit","when":"The manager enters ration details and ingredient proportions"},{"given":"The ration service returns nutrition values and calculated ingredient-mix cost","id":"AC-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned nutrition values and calculated cost per pound","when":"The ration screen renders the response"},{"given":"An authorized ration manager has selected nutrition requirements and candidate mixes","id":"AC-8.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen identifies the returned lowest-cost mix that meets the selected requirements and displays its nutrition and cost values with a separate save action","when":"The manager runs optimization"},{"given":"An optimized candidate is displayed and the user has not selected a save action, or a user without ration-management access opens the ration screen","id":"AC-8.4","level":"ui","then":"The candidate is displayed without being shown as a saved ration, and the unauthorized user's screen displays existing rations without create, revise, optimize, or approve actions","when":"The screen renders"},{"given":"The optimization response indicates that no candidate mix meets the selected nutrition requirements","id":"AC-8.5","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays that no mix qualifies and does not show an enabled save action for a qualifying mix","when":"The manager views the optimization result"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions, display ingredient proportions, nutrition and cost values, and present the lowest-cost candidate mix meeting user-selected nutritional requirements without saving it until the user chooses to do so.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-5","ASM-6","ASM-20","ASM-29","Q-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized planner selects a date, pen, bunk rate, ration, and animal count","id":"AC-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The plan request contains those selected values and the screen displays the returned plan's date, pen, assigned lot or lots, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status","when":"The planner submits the plan"},{"given":"A user lacks planning access and opens feed planning","id":"AC-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays existing plans without plan-generation or plan-adjustment actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let authorized planners generate or adjust dated pen-level feed plans from bunk rates, ration assignments, and animal counts, and display the returned plan details and execution status.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-8","ASM-20","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A saved plan's pen count, bunk rate, animal count, or ration assignment changes after generation","id":"AC-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved plan unchanged and a review flag","when":"The user opens the plan"},{"given":"An authorized planner opens a plan flagged for review","id":"AC-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows authorized confirm-update and regenerate actions","when":"The plan screen renders"},{"given":"An authorized planner confirms an update or regenerates a flagged plan","id":"AC-10.3","level":"ui","then":"The plan request contains the selected action and the screen displays the response status and returned plan","when":"The planner submits the selected action"},{"given":"An operator is assigned to the plan's pen","id":"AC-10.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned status value for that pen's plan","when":"The operator updates the execution status"},{"given":"Actual bunk intake differs from the saved plan","id":"AC-10.5","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays actual intake and variance while the saved plan values remain unchanged","when":"The user views the feeding plan and activity"},{"given":"An operator is not assigned to the plan's pen and the screen renders using the operator's returned permissions","id":"AC-10.6","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the current status and does not show an enabled status-update action","when":"The operator opens the plan"},{"given":"The service refuses a status update submitted by an operator who is not assigned to the plan's pen","id":"AC-10.7","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned refusal error and the current plan status remains displayed","when":"The operator submits the status update"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall flag a saved plan for review when relevant inputs change, retain its saved values until an authorized planner confirms an update or regenerates it, allow assigned-pen operators to update execution status while withholding enabled status-update actions from other operators and displaying returned refusals for rejected updates, and show intake variance without automatically rewriting the saved plan.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-8","ASM-19","ASM-30","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operational user enters feeding date, pen, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and status for a pen containing one or more lots","id":"AC-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The feeding request contains the entered fields and a delivered-quantity allocation for each affected lot, and the screen displays the response status and returned event fields including the lot allocations","when":"The user submits the feeding event"},{"given":"A successful feeding response contains calculated values","id":"AC-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumed by ingredient, and cumulative lot feed consumption and cost","when":"The event screen renders the response"},{"given":"A successful feeding response contains planned quantity of 100 pounds, actual delivered quantity of 115 pounds, and a returned variance value of 15 pounds","id":"AC-11.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned variance value of 15 pounds","when":"The event screen renders the response"},{"given":"A feeding response includes actual delivered quantity and an inventory movement","id":"AC-11.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays stock consumption for the delivered quantity and known wastage as a separate movement rather than added delivered feed","when":"The event screen renders the response"},{"given":"The service refuses a feeding event because available stock is insufficient","id":"AC-11.5","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned stock error and does not display the event as saved","when":"The user submits the event"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens feeding activity","id":"AC-11.6","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays existing activity without an action to record a feeding event","when":"The screen renders"},{"given":"A feeding-event save request times out without a definitive response","id":"AC-11.7","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays that the save outcome is unknown, retains the submitted event fields, and disables resubmission until the user refreshes the activity list","when":"The web app handles the timeout"},{"given":"A save timed out and the user refreshes the activity list, which returns an event matching the submitted feeding date, pen, lot allocations, ration, planned quantity, delivered quantity, and status","id":"AC-11.8","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned matching event and sends no duplicate save request","when":"The refreshed list is displayed"},{"given":"A save timed out and the user refreshes the activity list, which returns no event matching the submitted feeding date, pen, lot allocations, ration, planned quantity, delivered quantity, and status","id":"AC-11.9","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays that no matching saved event was returned and enables the user to submit the retained event","when":"The refreshed list is displayed"},{"given":"A user has returned permission to correct or void saved feeding events","id":"AC-11.10","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows correction and void actions","when":"The user opens a saved feeding event"},{"given":"A user lacks returned permission to correct or void saved feeding events","id":"AC-11.11","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the event without enabled correction or void actions","when":"The user opens a saved feeding event"},{"given":"An authorized user submits a correction and the service returns the corrected event with updated inventory movement and lot totals","id":"AC-11.12","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned corrected event, inventory movement, and lot consumption and cost totals","when":"The correction response is displayed"},{"given":"An authorized user submits a void and the service returns the voided event with updated inventory movement and lot totals","id":"AC-11.13","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned void status, inventory movement, and lot consumption and cost totals","when":"The void response is displayed"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot, including per-lot allocations when a pen contains multiple lots, display the returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, feeding status, and lot-level consumption and cost totals, display a returned stock error when insufficient stock prevents saving, provide permission-controlled correction and void actions for saved feeding events, and prevent duplicate resubmission while an uncertain save outcome is reconciled.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","I-6","ASM-4","ASM-9","ASM-10","ASM-11","ASM-20","ASM-28","ASM-31","ASM-32","ASM-34","Q-5","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user enters a lot weight measurement","id":"AC-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The measurement request contains lot, date, animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight when entered, and notes, and the screen displays the response status and saved measurement","when":"The user submits the measurement"},{"given":"The weight response contains multiple measurements","id":"AC-12.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays returned measurements in date order with weight gain since the previous measurement where returned","when":"A user views the lot's weight history"},{"given":"A user without measurement-entry access opens a lot's weight history","id":"AC-12.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the measurement time series without an enabled add-measurement action","when":"The screen renders"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let authorized livestock or operations users add lot weight measurements and display each lot's measurement history as a time-ordered series with returned measurement and gain information.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-12","Q-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The lot metrics response contains receiving date, entry and current average weight, feed totals, feed cost, target weight, ADG, and projected ship date","id":"AC-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date","when":"A user opens lot performance"},{"given":"A lot has no positive ADG available","id":"AC-13.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the projected ship date as unavailable","when":"The user opens the lot performance screen"},{"given":"A feeding or weight record is saved and the service returns updated lot metrics","id":"AC-13.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the recalculated metric values returned for the updated records","when":"The user opens or refreshes lot performance after the save"},{"given":"The lot metrics response contains days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date for a lot with multiple animals","id":"AC-13.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each metric value returned by the service without substituting a web-calculated value","when":"A user opens lot performance"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics for days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh displayed metrics after feeding or weight records change.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-6","I-8","ASM-13","ASM-20","ASM-33"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The insights service returns a feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestion and its supporting trend data or rule","id":"AC-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the suggestion and its returned explanation or cited basis","when":"The user opens lot insights"},{"given":"A suggestion is displayed and the user has not chosen an action","id":"AC-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved feed plan unchanged and does not change the sale date","when":"The user views the suggestion"},{"given":"An authorized planner chooses to act on a displayed suggestion","id":"AC-14.3","level":"ui","then":"The change request contains the planner's selected action and the screen displays the response status","when":"The planner submits the corresponding change"},{"given":"A user without planning access views a suggestion or the service refuses that user's attempted plan change","id":"AC-14.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen does not show an enabled plan-change action, or displays the returned refusal error, and the saved feed plan remains unchanged","when":"The user opens lot insights or submits the change request"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall present explainable rule-based suggestions for feeding adjustments or sale timing based on lot weight-gain trends and leave any resulting plan or sale change to an authorized planner's explicit action.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-8","I-9","ASM-18","ASM-19"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard service returns yard, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and performance values","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current